    "**No feasibility decision beyond §5.** I4 and I6 are necessary conditions. A target that passes them may be unreachable for this column (finite stages, energy), and an unreached target (§7.3) is not evidence of infeasibility: U1 and U2 have regular roots the path from S02's endpoint does not reach.",
    "**No convergence claim beyond the registered paths.** S02's endpoint is ill-conditioned when it already holds the specified component almost entirely in one product (U1), and a straight path from it can cross an unphysical region (U2: negative reflux at a total condenser whose `φ` is free). Only J1–J8's and the V-sets' straight paths are measured; Q-S06-2.",
